All 262 tests pass, including the new email-duplicate test. 

## Summary

I implemented the change in the V1 owner creation endpoint (`addOwner`) in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. When a request supplies an email, after it's normalized (trimmed, lower-cased), the controller now checks all existing owners and returns **409 Conflict** if any other owner already uses the same email (compared case-insensitively):

```java
owner.setEmail(email);
for (Owner existing : this.clinicService.findAllOwners()) {
    if (existing.getEmail() != null && email.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getEmail())) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
}
```

This follows the existing conventions in the file (the same `findAllOwners()` iteration pattern already used for the telephone-duplicate and city-capacity checks). The check sits after email validation, so an invalid email still yields 400 as before.

I also added a test, `createOwnerDuplicateEmailReturnsConflict`, that creates an owner with `George.Mailer@Example.com` and confirms a second creation with `george.mailer@example.com` (differing only in case) is rejected with 409. The full suite — 262 tests — is green.

